      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture. The test verifies that `reset()` throws an `IOException` when the stream was marked with a negative read limit (meaning the read limit is immediately exceeded). I'll improve readability by using `Integer.MAX_VALUE` instead of the magic literal, naming the negative limit, and adding a descriptive test name.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored test replaces the magic literal `2147483647L` with `(long) Integer.MAX_VALUE`, extracts `-645` into a named constant `negativeReadLimit`, renames the test method to `test06_resetThrowsWhenMarkedWithNegativeReadLimit`, and adds a Javadoc comment explaining the scenario — all without changing any method calls, arguments, or expected outcomes."
